<!-- better  -->
use the prev studied heapfiy , heapfiy sort and buildheap approach here 


basically we first do buildheap 

then we know that 1st element of heap is 1st smallest
so we count , cnt++

then we swap it with last index 

and again do heapify for top values as its only not in its correct place other are 

now first element is the second smallest 
so we do cnt++

and continue this process until cnt reaches the kth value 

if reached then return the top element

TC - buildheap (n)  + loop till k * hepify single call (klogn - because its running till k only worst case k=n , so nlogn 
but we can't always assume that k will be n as k is variable)

~ n + klogn


total tc is buildheap + heapsort 
        
here we are not excluding n and simply say klogn is the largest
because k is a variable 
and it does change and affect overall tc
eg
k = 1 
n = 1000
tc = 1000 + 1*10

here larger term is n not klogn



